;;; hilbert-onb.scm -- ORTHONORMAL BASES of a complex inner product / Hilbert space.
;;; Agent BA-ONB, 2026-11-09 (scratchpad/triage/BA-ONB.md).  Helper prefix: onb-.
;;; Vocabulary: structure-library/hilbert-onb-vocab.scm (IS-ORTHONORMAL-SET,
;;; IS-ORTHONORMAL-FAMILY, IS-ORTHONORMAL-BASIS).  Every theorem bills modulo 0; nothing is
;;; asserted.  Source: th-main.pdf s.2.1.
;;;
;;;   onb-exists                       every CIPS has an orthonormal basis (Zorn)
;;;   onb-extension                    every orthonormal family extends to a basis (Ex. 2.3)
;;;   bessel-inequality                sum_i |<x,e_i>|^2 <= <x,x>, the sum in [0,+inf] (Prop 2.5)
;;;   summable-of-cauchy-net           the Cauchy criterion for SUMS-TO in a complete
;;;                                    normed abelian group (general; no inner product)
;;;   onb-expansion                    x = sum_i <x,e_i> e_i unconditionally, H Hilbert (Prop 2.10)
;;;   parseval-identity                sum_i |<x,e_i>|^2 = <x,x>, H Hilbert (Prop 2.6, the identity)
;;;
;;; Lemmas on the way: onb-unit-scale-identity, onb-unit-multiple (the unit multiple of a
;;; nonzero vector), onb-orthonormal-chain-union, onb-orthonormal-insert,
;;; onb-complete-orthonormal-set-exists (Zorn on orthonormal SETS containing a given one),
;;; onb-image-orthonormal, onb-of-complete-orthonormal-set, onb-ip-normed-ag-iden,
;;; onb-partial-sums (finite-set induction: Y_w, <Y_w,e_k>, P_w, <Y_w,Y_w> = <Y_w,x> = P_w),
;;; onb-bessel-partial, onb-cauchy-net-choice-seq, onb-partial-nested, onb-partial-diff,
;;; onb-expansion-cauchy-net, onb-coef-limit, onb-residual.
;;;
;;; Notation in the comments: Y_w = FINSUM over w of the coefficient family
;;; cf = i |-> <x,e_i> e_i in the abelian group of v; P_w = FINSUM over w of
;;; gq = i |-> |<x,e_i>|^2 in RR-POS-STAR-ADD-MONOID; E = ESUM(gq).
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW [hilbert-projection + 1, end).  lo: the latest citations are
;;; hilbert-projection's (ip-metric-space-dist, ip-normed-ag-opr / -inv,
;;; cips-ip-magnitude-le, cips-eq-of-dist-sq-zero, cips-ip-neg-right); the others are earlier
;;; (rb2-esum-approx in rake-asm-b2, zorn-lemma in zorn-route-two, the NAG metric laws in
;;; rake-norm-metrics, the ESUM laws in rake-esum-defined, the finsum laws).  hi: nothing in
;;; the tree cites these names.  Library: analysis.  The slices it was probed in are
;;; scratchpad/baonb-1109/onb-[a-i].scm.

